       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled daily dose of oral ibuprofen for adults (3,200 mg/day). A dose that high carries a serious risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even when kidney and liver function are normal.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n- **400 mg four times daily** (1,600 mg/day), a common regimen for mild to moderate pain.\n- **800 mg three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), a common regimen for inflammatory conditions or higher pain levels.\n- **800 mg four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum dose.\n- **1600 mg per day** divided into a different schedule.\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that. Tell me the clinical rationale too, and I'll add it to the order note. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away."
