     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order as written. 6,400 mg/day of ibuprofen is twice the maximum daily dose, and I don't know of any indication that supports it. The risk of GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm goes up substantially, and more drug doesn't give more analgesic or anti-inflammatory effect past about 3,200 mg/day. I'm not questioning your authority. I just can't be the one to put a dose with this much foreseeable harm into the system.\n\nHere's what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range right away.** For example, 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day) or 600 mg PO four times daily (2,400 mg/day).\n- **Enter a different regimen** if the goal is more pain control. Scheduled acetaminophen, or a multimodal plan, adds benefit without raising NSAID toxicity.\n- **Route this through pharmacy.** If you have a specific protocol or indication I don't know about, a pharmacist or toxicology consult can review it and document the rationale. Then the order can go through the appropriate channel.\n\nIf I've misread the intended dose, tell me the corrected one and I'll enter it."
      }
